<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I0cf9fae272292855ef86ce79a6a4236f030bffd6" commit="db0e833839c2a4a9f90610ccdb6805dc3c82b758" commit_message="UPSTREAM: google/chromeec: Add new helper function to read MKBP events  This change adds a new helper function google_chromeec_get_mkbp_event that allows coreboot to query EC for the next available MKBP event.  BUG=b:67872897 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Change-Id: I0cf9fae272292855ef86ce79a6a4236f030bffd6 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Original-Commit-Id: e01bf6452fb215a4598fb0edcdbf6e532ee6505f Original-Change-Id: Ia6d64586ca62378d08025c96c2689c00c816041f Original-Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/22007 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) &lt;no-reply@coreboot.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/724925 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="724925" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/25/724925/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="Idd987f34cd136292a8d241d62bb5fef298a1bbc3" commit="4734687b3d5d903f3e81692b4e18ab8b11daf509" commit_message="UPSTREAM: google/chromeec: Drain all MKBP events while clearing host events  EC maintains a FIFO of all MKBP events and sets host event whenever a new entry is added to the FIFO. Clearing only the host event for MKBP creates an inconsistent state where there are pending MKBP events in the FIFO but host event for MKBP is cleared. In order to maintain a consistent view, host should clear all MKBP events in the FIFO if host event is being cleared.  This change drains out all the MKBP events in the FIFO when clear_pending_events is called.  BUG=b:67872897 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified by adding debug logs in EC to verify that all the MKBP events that occur before clear_pending_events is called get cleared from the FIFO.  Change-Id: Idd987f34cd136292a8d241d62bb5fef298a1bbc3 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Original-Commit-Id: c1ca65df3f3d4d98820f9431a2e41b446928d8dd Original-Change-Id: I131722dc01608dff30230fe341e6b23ae4cc409e Original-Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/22005 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) &lt;no-reply@coreboot.org&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Paul Menzel &lt;paulepanter@users.sourceforge.net&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/724926 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="724926" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/26/724926/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I649129812bcee321eb5341ab857eb1e6610b7ad7" commit="03dd507032de3083988c06562b675b04d65d4567" commit_message="linux-headers: Export media v4l metadata buffer type  This is used by video device for meta data type such as V4L2_META_FMT_IPU3_STAT_3A etc.  BUG=b:65647199 TEST=emerge, check /build/${BOARD}/usr/include/linux  Change-Id: I649129812bcee321eb5341ab857eb1e6610b7ad7 Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/679200 Commit-Ready: Tianshu Qiu &lt;tian.shu.qiu@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="679200" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/00/679